  "summary": "The study fabricated two freestanding Ti3C2Tx-film electrodes: an undoped Ti3C2Tx control and an N\u2013Ti3C2Tx film treated with hydrazine hydrate. Both originated from LiF/HCl-etched Ti3AlC2 and were tested in 1 M H2SO4 using a three-electrode cell. The primary N\u2013Ti3C2Tx film delivered the best reported capacitance, 340 F g\u22121 at 2 mV s\u22121 and 1.35 mg cm\u22122 loading, versus 234 F g\u22121 for the undoped film under the same stated conditions. The N-doped film was approximately 5 \u03bcm thick; numerical flake size, d-spacing, BET surface area, porosity, pore diameter, and volumetric/areal capacitance were not reported."
